# What must not ride along to a public URL.
#
# The Vercel CLI does not read .gitignore, and the first production deploy of this project
# published `local/fleet.json` — a scan of one laptop's home directory, 76 repository names and
# their paths — on a URL anyone could open. The pages looked right, which is why nobody would have
# checked. This file is the reason that cannot happen again.

.env
.env.local

# One machine's scan. The hosted fleet page uses the bundled portable one instead.
local/

# Built locally, rebuildable with `npm run index:build`, and large.
index/data/

node_modules/
.git/
.vercel
*.log
.DS_Store
